diff --strip-trailing-cr -ruN UnitXP_SP3-v89_original/unitxp_sp3/MOONSTONE_MARKS.md UnitXP_SP3-v89_src/unitxp_sp3/MOONSTONE_MARKS.md
--- UnitXP_SP3-v89_original/unitxp_sp3/MOONSTONE_MARKS.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ UnitXP_SP3-v89_src/unitxp_sp3/MOONSTONE_MARKS.md	2026-08-01 15:17:22.913247083 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+# Moonstone-style ground markers
+
+This source tree adds seven ground markers to UnitXP_SP3 v89 while preserving the
+Lua API expected by `UnitXP_SP3_Addon`.
+
+## Lua API
+
+```lua
+-- Place/replace the selected color at the world position under the mouse cursor.
+-- On success returns x, y, z, normalizedColor.
+UnitXP("2DMark", "red")
+UnitXP("2DMark", "yellow")
+UnitXP("2DMark", "green")
+UnitXP("2DMark", "blue")
+UnitXP("2DMark", "purple")
+UnitXP("2DMark", "orange")
+UnitXP("2DMark", "white")
+
+-- Place/replace a marker received through addon communication.
+UnitXP("RemoteMark", "red", x, y, z, sender)
+
+-- Remove every marker.
+UnitXP("ClearAllMarks")
+
+-- Returns count, marksTable. Each entry has color/x/y/z fields.
+local count, marks = UnitXP("QueryMarks")
+```
+
+## Visual design
+
+The marker is an additive screen-space overlay inspired by Elder's Moonstone:
+
+- broad low-alpha outer moonlight;
+- narrower colored body;
+- pearly near-white center core;
+- soft top and bottom fades;
+- pulsing ground halo and ring;
+- physical world-size projection plus a pixel-width clamp, preventing the marker
+  from becoming a huge opaque wall at close range;
+- no line-of-sight occlusion, matching the existing 2D marker behavior.
+
+The implementation uses no external texture and allocates no persistent Direct3D
+resources. It renders with `DrawPrimitiveUP` and restores the complete D3D9 state
+before returning.
+
+## Source changes
+
+- `worldMarks.cpp` / `worldMarks.h`: placement, storage, rendering and query logic.
+- `dllmain.cpp`: UnitXP command handlers.
+- `sceneBegin_sceneEnd.cpp`: draw call before D3DXSprite combat text.
+- `Makefile`: adds `worldMarks.cpp`.
+
+## Build note
+
+The upstream Makefile expects the local directories `xwinSDK` and `d3d9x_headers`,
+which are not bundled in the v89 source archive. Use the same toolchain and
+dependency layout described by the upstream project before running `make`.
